 - Writes require the `contributor` or `manager` role in the project. Users who can read but not write get 403.
 - Contributors may only modify tasks assigned to themselves, and may not reassign tasks. Managers may modify any task.
 - Only managers may delete tasks.
-- Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
+- Freezing: only managers may freeze a project (others 403). Freezing sets every
+  member's role to `viewer`, managers included, in one transaction. Afterwards
+  nobody can change the project's tasks (members get 403, org admins still
+  cannot write). The project's other data and other projects are unchanged.
+  A frozen project has no manager left, so a second freeze is 403. There is no
+  unfreeze endpoint.
+- Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work). This includes freezing.
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
